# Project operating rules

- Treat all GTM data in this repository as synthetic demonstration data. Never imply access to Red Hat, customer, or confidential data.
- Never add secrets, passwords, tokens, account identifiers, or connection strings to source code, prompts, logs, screenshots, or documentation.
- Prefer the smallest reviewable change. Do not rewrite unrelated code.
- For Python changes, preserve deterministic outputs and add or update tests.
- For analytical calculations, state assumptions and verify results against source data.
- For Snowflake SQL, use readable CTEs, explicit column names, safe identifiers, and read-only queries by default.
- Do not execute destructive SQL or upload data unless the human owner explicitly confirms the target and action.
- Separate observed facts, interpretations, risks, and recommended actions in stakeholder summaries.
- AI suggestions are proposals. The human owner reviews diffs, runs tests, inspects outputs, and owns the final decision.
